<section class="doc-section" id="feedback">
    <div class="section-heading"><span class="section-index">12</span><div><p class="eyebrow">OPEN SOURCE &amp; COMMUNITY</p><h2>Project &amp; community</h2></div></div>
    <p>ToastKit is open source under the MIT License. Contributions are welcome: report a bug, share an idea, improve the docs or examples, or send a focused pull request.</p>
    <div class="info-grid">
      <article><span class="pill red">ISSUES</span><h3>Bugs and feature requests</h3><p>Use a structured form for reproducible bugs or a specific feature request.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/DavidRicardoWilde/swiftui-toastkit/issues/new/choose">Open a GitHub issue ↗</a></p></article>
      <article><span class="pill violet">DISCUSSIONS</span><h3>Questions and ideas</h3><p>Use Discussions for usage questions, general feedback, and ideas that need conversation before becoming an issue.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/DavidRicardoWilde/swiftui-toastkit/discussions">Open GitHub Discussions ↗</a></p></article>
    </div>
    <div class="info-grid">
      <article><span class="pill neutral">CONTRIBUTE</span><h3>Help shape ToastKit</h3><p>Read the contribution guide for project conventions and pull request notes.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/DavidRicardoWilde/swiftui-toastkit/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">Read CONTRIBUTING.md ↗</a></p></article>
      <article><span class="pill neutral">TAGS &amp; RELEASES</span><h3>Browse version history</h3><p>Tags identify the source for each version. GitHub Releases may include packaged notes and assets.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/DavidRicardoWilde/swiftui-toastkit/tags">Browse tags ↗</a> · <a href="https://github.com/DavidRicardoWilde/swiftui-toastkit/releases">Releases ↗</a></p></article>
      <article><span class="pill amber">CHANGELOG</span><h3>What changed</h3><p>See the changes grouped by the repository’s published tags.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/DavidRicardoWilde/swiftui-toastkit/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md">Read the changelog ↗</a></p></article>
    </div>
    <p>When reporting a bug, include a minimal Swift example, steps to reproduce, what happened, and what you expected instead. The example may intentionally contain incorrect or non-compiling code. Add screenshots or a screen recording for visual problems, and include iOS/iPadOS, device or simulator, Xcode, Swift, and ToastKit versions.</p>
    <p>Use comments on an existing issue or discussion for follow-up, clarification, and progress updates. For pull requests, focused changes with a brief explanation and validation notes are easiest to review.</p>
  </section>
